<% content_for :title, "Terms of Service" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "The rules for using Path Aviator: accounts, the Free and Pro plans, payments through Dodo Payments, AI-generated plans, acceptable use and liability." %>

<div class="legal-summary">
  <p><strong>The short version.</strong> Use Path Aviator to plan and track your own learning. Plans are written by AI from real resources, so check them with care: we can’t promise a job or that every link stays up. Pro renews until you cancel, and you can cancel any time. You own your notes. Don’t abuse the service.</p>
</div>

<%= legal_section "Agreement" do %>
  <p>These terms are an agreement between you and <strong><%= Legal.owner_name %></strong>, the individual who runs Path Aviator (“we”, “us”). By creating an account or using the site you accept them, together with our <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %> and <%= link_to "Refund & Cancellation Policy", refunds_path %>.</p>
  <p>You must be 18 or over to create an account.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Your account" do %>
  <ul>
    <li>Use an email address you can receive mail at, and keep your password to yourself. One account is for one person.</li>
    <li>You’re responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us straight away if you think someone else has signed in.</li>
    <li>The public demo account is shared and reset every night. Don’t put anything personal in it.</li>
  </ul>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Plans and payment" do %>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free</strong> lets you plan <%= pluralize(Plan.free.monthly_generations, "new path") %> a month (re-planning a path counts as one), with progress tracking, notes and share links.</li>
    <li><strong>Pro</strong> is a subscription, billed monthly or yearly at the prices on the Pricing page, in Indian rupees or US dollars. Pro includes unlimited paths under fair use: if usage looks automated or abusive, we may slow it down or ask you to stop.</li>
    <li><strong>Dodo Payments is the merchant of record.</strong> When you buy Pro you buy it from Dodo Payments, which takes the payment, issues your invoice and collects any GST, VAT or sales tax.</li>
    <li><strong>Pro renews automatically</strong> at the end of each billing period until you cancel. You can cancel at any time; see the <%= link_to "Refund & Cancellation Policy", refunds_path %> for what happens next and when you can get your money back.</li>
    <li>If we change Pro’s price, we’ll email you at least 30 days before your next renewal at the new price.</li>
  </ul>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "AI-generated plans" do %>
  <p>Paths are generated by an AI model from the details you give and then checked by our software. They can still contain mistakes, outdated advice or links that stop working. We check links, but the courses, videos and docs we link to belong to other people, and we don’t control or endorse them.</p>
  <p>Path Aviator helps you plan and keep going. It doesn’t guarantee that you’ll learn a skill, pass an interview or get a job.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Acceptable use" do %>
  <p>Please don’t:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use scripts, bots or multiple accounts to generate paths or get around limits;</li>
    <li>try to break, overload or probe the security of the service, or access other people’s data;</li>
    <li>use the AI planner to produce content that’s illegal, harmful or unrelated to learning;</li>
    <li>publish anything in shared pages or certificates that you don’t have the right to share, or that misrepresents what you’ve done;</li>
    <li>resell or copy the service as your own.</li>
  </ul>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Your content" do %>
  <p>Your goals, notes and evidence links are yours. You give us permission to store and process them only to run Path Aviator for you. When you turn on a share link or publish a certificate, anyone with that link can see what the page shows, until you turn it off.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Our content" do %>
  <p>The Path Aviator name, design, curated study plans and site text belong to us. The application’s source code is published under the MIT License on <a href="https://github.com/MeghaKoshti/path-aviator" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>, and that licence applies to the code.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Availability and changes" do %>
  <p>We work to keep Path Aviator running, but it’s provided “as is”, without a guarantee that it will always be available or error-free. We may change or remove features. If we ever stop offering Pro, we’ll give you at least 30 days’ notice and refund any prepaid time you haven’t used.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Liability" do %>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, our total liability to you for any claim about Path Aviator is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. We aren’t liable for indirect losses such as lost opportunities or lost data. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer protection law that can’t be waived.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Ending your account" do %>
  <p>You can delete your account at any time from Settings. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms, and we’ll tell you why unless the law prevents it. If we close a paid account without it having broken these terms, we’ll refund unused prepaid time.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Law and disputes" do %>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. Courts in <%= Legal::JURISDICTION %> have jurisdiction, but if you’re a consumer you keep any right to bring a claim where you live. Please contact us first: most problems are quicker to sort out by email.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Changes to these terms" do %>
  <p>When we change these terms we update the date at the top. For changes that matter, we’ll email you at least 14 days before they take effect. If you keep using Path Aviator after that, the new terms apply.</p>
<% end %>

<%= legal_section "Contact" do %>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <%= support_mail_link(subject: "Terms question") %>.</p>
<% end %>
